 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 03_sp500_application : Application aux pertes extrêmes (S&P500) — tutoriel en français\n",
    "\n",
    "Objectifs :\n",
    "- Télécharger historique S&P500 via yfinance, calculer les pertes (drawdowns / retours négatifs).\n",
    "- Prétraiter (peaks-over-threshold ou block-maxima) et entraîner un GAN/WGAN-GP sur les pertes.\n",
    "- Évaluer la qualité sur quantiles extrêmes et estimateur de Hill.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Imports\n",
    "import yfinance as yf\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "from src.data_utils import download_sp500_returns\n",
    "from src.train import train_gan\n",
    "from src.eval_extremes import compare_quantiles, plot_qq_tail, hill_estimator\n",
    "import torch\n",
    "device = torch.device('cuda' if torch.cuda.is_available() else 'cpu')\n",
    "print('Device:', device)\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1) Télécharger les données et construire série de pertes" 
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "losses = download_sp500_returns(start='2000-01-01')\n",
    "print('Observations losses:', len(losses))\n",
    "losses.head()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Visualiser histogramme des pertes (en échelle linéaire)\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(8,4))\n",
    "plt.hist(losses.values, bins=200, density=True)\n",
    "plt.xlim(0, 0.2)\n",
    "plt.title('Histogramme des pertes (S&P500 daily losses)')\n",
    "plt.show()\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2) Prétraitement : peaks-over-threshold (POT) simple\n",
    "\n",
    "On choisit un seuil (par ex. quantile 95%) et on prend les pertes au-dessus du seuil (les "exceedances")."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "thresh = np.quantile(losses.values, 0.95)\n",
    "exceed = losses[losses > thresh].values\n",
    "print('Seuil (95%):', thresh, 'Nombre dépassant:', len(exceed))\n",
    "plt.hist(exceed, bins=100, density=True)\n",
    "plt.title('Distribution des exceedances (POT)')\n",
    "plt.show()\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3) Entraîner un GAN simple sur les exceedances (log-transform optionnelle)\n",
    "\n",
    "Pour plus de stabilité, on peut entraîner sur log(exceed) comme dans les notebooks précédents.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Préparer données (log)\n",
    "exceed = exceed[~np.isinf(exceed)]\n",
    "data_log = np.log(exceed)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Entraîner GAN vanilla rapide (tutoriel)\n",
    "G, D, hist = train_gan(data_log, z_dim=16, n_epochs=80, batch_size=64, lr=1e-4, device=device)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Générer et comparer\n",
    "G.eval()\n",
    "with torch.no_grad():\n",
    "    z = torch.randn(10000, 16, device=device)\n",
    "    gen = G(z).cpu().numpy()\n",
    "gen_exp = np.exp(gen)\n",
    "real_exp = np.exp(data_log)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(compare_quantiles(real_exp, gen_exp, qs=[0.90, 0.95, 0.99]))\n",
    "plot_qq_tail(real_exp, gen_exp, p_min=0.9, p_max=0.999, n=100)\n",
    "gamma_real, se_real = hill_estimator(real_exp, k=min(100, len(real_exp)-1))\n",
    "gamma_gen, se_gen = hill_estimator(gen_exp, k=min(100, len(gen_exp)-1))\n",
    "print('Hill real:', gamma_real, 'Hill gen:', gamma_gen)\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4) Exercices et analyses supplémentaires\n",
    "\n",
    "- Essaye WGAN-GP (notebook 02) sur ces exceedances : compare les quantiles et l'estimateur de Hill.\n",
    "- Essaie d'entraîner sans log transform et compare les résultats.\n",
    "- Expérimente différents seuils POT (90%, 95%, 99%) et observe la stabilité de l'estimation des queues.\n"
   ]
  }
